CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*first_mapping)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct shared_rcu_mapping)...)
#244: FILE: security/selinux/ss/services.c:2080:
+		first_mapping = kzalloc(sizeof(struct shared_rcu_mapping),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

